## 4. Review Methods & Required Materials by Phase

| Phase | Review Form | Required Materials |
|---|---|---|
| **Preliminary & National Review** | Materials submitted by teams | [Template 1] Word file + optional PPT, design files, demo videos. Must include: background & value of the solution, application scenarios, actual problem addressed, innovation highlights (e.g. AI application scenario innovation), dataset selection & data processing, explanation of key code snippets, and **quantifiable indicators** demonstrating effectiveness |
| **Regional Competition** | 15-min presentation + 5-min panel Q&A | [Template 2] PPT + visual demo page URL + **complete application code** + relevant datasets + README (reproduction/deployment steps) + screenshot proving open-sourcing on a community (e.g. GitHub, Gitee). **The committee will attempt to reproduce your results — a mismatch disqualifies the team from advancement and awards.** |
| **Global Final** | 15-min presentation + 5-min panel Q&A | Same as Regional, plus explanation of application/deployment progress. Max one team per country/region. |

