## 5. Review Criteria Weighting by Phase

| Criterion | Preliminary & National | Regional | Global Final |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Innovation** — AI application scenario innovation, differentiation from existing solutions | 60% | 40% | 40% |
| **Application Value** — addresses real needs, scalable/replicable for real-world deployment, technically complete & feasible | 40% | 35% | 30% |
| **Completeness & Demonstrability** — complete, logically structured materials covering background, technical approach, data, code, performance; interactive demo required | — | 15% | 15% |
| **Application & Implementation Progress** — commercial/non-profit deployment progress, community recognition (e.g. GitHub stars) post-open-sourcing | — | — | 10% |
| **Presentation & Panel Performance** — fluency, clarity of answers | — | 10% | 5% |

**Reading the trend:** Innovation dominates at Preliminary (gets you in the door). From Regional onward, weight shifts hard toward a *working, reproducible, demonstrable* system — the story alone stops being enough.

