## 7. Organizer's Presentation Tips (from the broadcast)

- **Fluent, confident English** — natural delivery, not reading off slides
- **Structure like a TED Talk:** Problem → Why It Matters → Innovation → Impact → Future
- **Pitch like Shark Tank:** convince judges the project is practical, valuable, scalable, and worth supporting
- **Creativity matters** — show what makes the solution different from existing approaches
- **Think global** 🌏 — design and present as something replicable and scalable internationally, not just for Malaysia or one university
- **Presentation is a strategy, not an obligation for everyone** — choose your strongest speaker(s) by English proficiency, confidence, technical depth, storytelling, and Q&A strength; not every team member needs to present
- **Everyone must know the project deeply** regardless of who presents — Q&A can go to anyone
- **Demonstrate where possible** — prototype, real use case, results, user feedback, measurable impact
- **End on one strong, memorable message** — why this innovation matters and what it could become globally
- **Overall framing:** *"Don't present it like a university assignment. Pitch it like an innovation that deserves to go global."*

