## 8. Reference Benchmark: HyperNeura (Senior Team, 2nd Place)

Included here as a calibration point — what a placing entry in this exact competition actually looked like.

**Team:** HyperNeura — Dr Azliza (advisor), Ammar, Aqil, Aidil — UiTM, entered via Huawei ICT Academy, SDG 10 (Reduced Inequalities) aligned.

**Tagline:** *"Speak Without Speaking, Hear Without Hearing"* — Empowering Communication, Redefining Connection.

**Problem framed:**
- 430 million people live with disabling hearing loss; 70–80% of deaf people face daily communication barriers; projected 2.5 billion with hearing loss by 2050
- Localized hook: Malaysia's 2027 school syllabus adds Sign Language (Bahasa Isyarat Malaysia) as an optional subject from Standard 1 — used as a timely local relevance point

**Solution:** HyperNeura — a smart wearable glove translating hand gestures to voice, and speech to text, in real time.
- **Sign-to-Speech:** translates Standard Sign Language (MySL/BIM) into the user's preferred spoken language
- **Speech-to-Text:** transcribes spoken language to a display for the user to read
- **Multilingual:** Bahasa Malaysia, English, Mandarin (more planned)
- Framed explicitly as "Bridging communication gap," tied to Huawei's *Intelligent World 2035* vision

**Hardware (prototype BOM):** LCD, ESP32, microphone, IMU sensor, speaker, battery, flex sensor ×5, rubber glove base

**Huawei-native technical pipeline (this is the standout element):**
- **Sign-to-Text model development:** sign language time-series dataset → flex sensor + IMU capture → **stored in Huawei OBS** → **model development in MindSpore** → **deployed via Huawei ModelArts**
- **System architecture:** gesture (flex + IMU) and speech (microphone) both feed into ESP32 → **ModelArts inference for gesture classification, hosted on Huawei ECS** + **Huawei Speech Kit API** for ASR (speech-to-text) and TTS (text-to-speech) → output to a second ESP32 driving an LCD display and speaker
- **Every layer of the ML/AI pipeline runs on a named Huawei product** — OBS, MindSpore, ModelArts, ECS, Speech Kit

**Reported results:** 94.7% accuracy; 1,464 training samples, 367 validation samples; dataset composed of time-series, flex sensor, and IMU sensor data

**Competitive positioning ("Why We Win" table):**
| Feature | HyperNeura | Existing product |
|---|---|---|
| Real-time sign-to-audio | Yes | Yes |
| Local sign language (BIM) | Yes | Needs manual add/train |
| Voice-to-text on-device | Yes (on glove) | Via mobile app only |
| Multilingual output | Yes | Yes |
| Malaysian speech recognition | Yes | No |
| Cost (prototype) | RM150 | ~RM12,000+ |

**Market slide:** global (700M projected hearing-loss by 2050, WHO; <1 interpreter per 1,000 DHH people, WFD 2018; global assistive tech market to USD 31.6B by 2027) cross-referenced against Malaysia-specific figures (44,500 registered deaf Malaysians, JKM 2022; only 60 interpreters nationwide, BERNAMA 2025) — go-to-market via direct sales, NGO/hospital/school partnerships, and CSR/government-grant subsidies.

**Human element:** two named "before/after" user personas (a mute child, a deaf mother) plus one real testimonial quote from a named person with a hearing impairment — used to close the emotional arc before the "Thank You" slide.

